e in this result.","B":"The imagined past result uses **would have prepared**.","C":"The perfect auxiliary have is missing.","D":"Would takes base have, not had."}}},{"id":"a1b3e4b5-2c63-532e-aa3f-57b8787dedb0","topicSlug":"third-mixed-conditionals","level":"B2","prompt":"Complete the present result of a mixed conditional: “If she had prepared the evening meal yesterday, she ____ free now.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"would is"},{"id":"B","text":"would be"},{"id":"C","text":"would have been"},{"id":"D","text":"would been"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Read **now**: the condition is past, but the result is present.","explanation":"The result is **now**, so use **would be**, while the past condition keeps had + participle.","keywords":["past-condition-present-result"],"skill":"past-condition-present-result","contextKey":"third-mixed-conditionals-49","fingerprint":"b6a3d276bd66af8e4ade32a3460bfa887b51c5d5ea0d6db7b54c4a19d73db15e","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-third-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Read **now**: the condition is past, but the result is present.","The result is **now**, so use **would be**, while the past condition keeps had + participle.","Choose **would be**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Is cannot follow would.","B":"The result is **now**, so use **would be**, while the past condition keeps had + participle.","C":"This would locate the imagined result in the past, contrary to the specified present result.","D":"Would requires base be unless have precedes been."}}},{"id":"9520a4c9-6830-506c-a029-10065aa75f5e","topicSlug":"third-mixed-conditionals","level":"B2","prompt":"Complete the past result of a mixed conditional: “If I were more organised, I ____ the evening meal yesterday.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"would had prepared"},{"id":"B","text":"would have preparing"},{"id":"C","text":"would have prepared"},{"id":"D","text":"would preparing"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Match the result to **yesterday**, not to the surface tense of the if-clause.","explanation":"The imagined result is yesterday, so it needs **would have prepared** despite the continuing-state condition.","keywords":["present-condition-past-result"],"skill":"present-condition-past-result","contextKey":"third-mixed-conditionals-49","fingerprint":"b00f0f9dc075fc5958f554f1d6b010e6a38b8f986ef58071092d33056cd97434","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-third-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Match the result to **yesterday**, not to the surface tense of the if-clause.","The imagined result is yesterday, so it needs **would have prepared** despite the continuing-state condition.","Choose **would have prepared**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"After would, use have rather than had.","B":"A past result in the simple perfect needs a past participle.","C":"The imagined result is yesterday, so it needs **would have prepared** despite the continuing-state condition.","D":"The result needs a perfect construction, not an unsupported -ing form."}}},{"id":"fdc02f2c-618e-5c85-a59f-8403ea8e94ea","topicSlug":"third-mixed-conditionals","level":"B2","prompt":"Use the third conditional: “If she ____ the rowing boat yesterday, we would have finished on time.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"has repaired"},{"id":"B","text":"had repaired"},{"id":"C","text":"would have repaired"},{"id":"D","text":"had repairing"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The condition concerns a **different past**, so use past perfect.","explanation":"The unreal past condition is **if + had + repaired**.","keywords":["unreal-past-condition"],"skill":"unreal-past-condition","contextKey":"third-mixed-conditionals-50","fingerprint":"b2c59e9464fb9f3f9af8197e4bfeb4d77cd86586cac04cc16e3b0858c32f7d0d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-third-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The condition concerns a **different past**, so use past perfect.","The unreal past condition is **if + had + repaired**.","Choose **had repaired**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Present perfect does not mark the unreal past condition requested.","B":"The unreal past condition is **if + had + repaired**.","C":"In the standard third conditional, would have belongs in the result clause.","D":"The past perfect requires a participle, not an -ing form."}}},{"id":"5f4e1242-1cd2-5174-a859-8b705cffe601","topicSlug":"third-mixed-conditionals","level":"B2","prompt":"Complete the third-conditional result: “If we had had more time yesterday, we ____ the rowing boat.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"would repaired"},{"id":"B","text":"would had repaired"},{"id":"C","text":"would have repairing"},{"id":"D","text":"would have repaired"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The result is also in an **unreal past**: use modal + have + participle.","explanation":"The imagined past result uses **would have repaired**.","keywords":["unreal-past-result"],"skill":"unreal-past-result","contextKey":"third-mixed-conditionals-50","fingerprint":"7441bf872d62439c574d92c5ae70993c14e33eb9cee97fe2c54f2f57724343ae","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-third-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The result is also in an **unreal past**: use modal + have + participle.","The imagined past result uses **would have repaired**.","Choose **would have repaired**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The perfect auxiliary have is missing.","B":"Would takes base have, not had.","C":"Have needs the past participle in this result.","D":"The imagined past result uses **would have repaired**."}}},{"id":"230dfc91-4649-5971-a21f-0b4a5d788cee","topicSlug":"third-mixed-conditionals","level":"B2","prompt":"Complete the present result of a mixed conditional: “If she had repaired the rowing boat yesterday, she ____ free now.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"would have been"},{"id":"B","text":"would been"},{"id":"C","text":"would is"},{"id":"D","text":"would be"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Read **now**: the condition is past, but the result is present.","explanation":"The result is **now**, so use **would be**, while the past condition keeps had + participle.","keywords":["past-condition-present-result"],"skill":"past-condition-present-result","contextKey":"third-mixed-conditionals-50","fingerprint":"ac7b1f64324bc11b2c4e5dd879168c1d2d86156942f055bed2354336058ed807","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-third-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Read **now**: the condition is past, but the result is present.","The result is **now**, so use **would be**, while the past condition keeps had + participle.","Choose **would be**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This would locate the imagined result in the past, contrary to the specified present result.","B":"Would requires base be unless have precedes been.","C":"Is cannot follow would.","D":"The result is **now**, so use **would be**, while the past condition keeps had + participle."}}},{"id":"259b5051-9c03-50df-aa42-ab2df6cef2bb","topicSlug":"third-mixed-conditionals","level":"B2","prompt":"Complete the past result of a mixed conditional: “If I were more organised, I ____ the rowing boat yesterday.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"would have repairing"},{"id":"B","text":"would have repaired"},{"id":"C","text":"would repairing"},{"id":"D","text":"would had repaired"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Match the result to **yesterday**, not to the surface tense of the if-clause.","explanation":"The imagined result is yesterday, so it needs **would have repaired** despite the continuing-state condition.","keywords":["present-condition-past-result"],"skill":"present-condition-past-result","contextKey":"third-mixed-conditionals-50","fingerprint":"c03aefecef9d9d752d9107d4c68099b3bc311dddf19a68e251241ea965b34e02","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-third-conditionals"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Match the result to **yesterday**, not to the surface tense of the if-clause.","The imagined result is yesterday, so it needs **would have repaired** despite the continuing-state condition.","Choose **would have repaired**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"A past result in the simple perfect needs a past participle.","B":"The imagined result is yesterday, so it needs **would have repaired** despite the continuing-state condition.","C":"The result needs a perfect construction, not an unsupported -ing form.","D":"After would, use have rather than had."}}}],"chapter":{"introduction":["Look back at an unreal past and connect past conditions with present consequences.","The form tells you how to build the sentence; the context tells you why that form is useful. Read each section with both questions in mind. The examples make one contrast at a time, while the practice mixes the skills so that you learn to recognise the pattern yourself."],"rules":[{"title":"An unreal past condition","explanation":"The usual **third conditional** imagines a past that did not happen. Use if + past perfect for the condition and would have + past participle for the result. The grammar shows both parts as alternatives to the actual past.","pattern":"If I **had called**, she **would have waited**.","commonMistakes":["Had and would have do different jobs. Do not routinely put would have in the if clause of this standard pattern."],"examples":["Use the third conditional: “If she **had prepared** the visitor guide yesterday, we would have finished on time.”","Use the third conditional: “If she **had restored** the old portrait yesterday, we would have finished on time.”"],"skill":"form"},{"title":"Possible and certain imagined results","explanation":"Could have or might have can replace would have when the imagined result is ability or possibility rather than the expected consequence. Keep the same perfect construction after the modal.","pattern":"We **might have won** if we had trained more.","commonMistakes":["Could have is not always interchangeable with would have; the strength or kind of result changes."],"examples":["Complete the third-conditional result: “If we had had more time yesterday, we **would have prepared** the visitor guide.”","Complete the third-conditional result: “If we had had more time yesterday, we **would have restored** the old portrait.”"],"skill":"meaning"},{"title":"Past condition, present result","explanation":"A mixed conditional can link an unreal past condition to a present result. The if-clause stays past perfect, but the present result normally uses would + base verb. Explicit time words help the reader follow the link.","pattern":"If I **had studied** medicine, I **would be** a doctor now.","commonMistakes":["Do not force have into a present result merely because the condition is past."],"examples":["Complete the present result of a mixed conditional: “If she had prepared the visitor guide yesterday, she **would be** free now.”","Complete the present result of a mixed conditional: “If she had restored the old portrait yesterday, she **would be** free now.”"],"skill":"contrast"},{"title":"Present condition, past result","explanation":"A continuing hypothetical state can explain an unreal past result. Use if + past simple for the imagined state and would have + participle for the past result. Match each clause to its own time instead of memorising one fixed pair.","pattern":"If I **were** more organised, I **would have remembered** yesterday.","commonMistakes":["The label mixed describes the time relationship, not an error in tense consistency."],"examples":["Complete the past result of a mixed conditional: “If I were more organised, I **would have prepared** the visitor guide yesterday.”","Complete the past result of a mixed conditional: “If I were more organised, I **would have restored** the old portrait yesterday.”"],"skill":"application"}],"recap":["If I **had called**, she **would have waited**.","We **might have won** if we had trained more.","If I **had studied** medicine, I **would be** a doctor now.","If I **were** more organised, I **would have remembered** yesterday."]},"stage":"4 · Connecting meanings","prerequisites":["conditionals"]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(version,slug) DO NOTHING;
